  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best singleprofile configuration is config_021 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat, acc=0.5353), with PCA clearly superior to scgpt for RNA and ViT-L slightly better than ResNet50. However, the multiprofile axis is completely unexplored—zero completed experiments use it. This is the largest remaining source of uncertainty about whether additional profile information (with aggregation) can push performance beyond the current ~0.535 ceiling. Question: Does adding multiple profiles with transformer aggregation, while holding the best-known encoders (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l) and fusion (concat) constant, improve over the singleprofile baseline? Why this experiment: config_042 is the most direct logical extension of config_021, changing only the profile setting and adding transformer aggregation. If it outperforms config_021, we confirm multiprofile is beneficial and can then explore aggregation variants; if it underperforms, we learn that the added complexity does not help and can redirect budget toward other axes (e.g., scvi_n200). Testing transformer first is informative because it is the most expressive aggregation—if even this fails to help, simpler aggregations (avgpool) are unlikely to succeed."
}

